# ---------------------------------------------------------------- raw MD data
# Trajectories and restarts are large and regenerable from the inputs that are
# published here. They stay on the machine that produced them.
*.lammpstrj
*.xyz
dump.*
restart.*
data.*
*.start.data
data.*_final
log.smoke*.lammps
log.short*.lammps
log.production*.lammps

# The one exception, and it is deliberate: the two minimized Stage G4 interface
# cells are the primary data behind Fig. 1, Table 1 and every stress number the
# manuscript quotes, so they ARE published, gzipped, under data/stageG4_clean/.
# The rule above does not match the .gz suffix today; this negation keeps that
# true if the pattern is ever tightened.
!data/stageG4_clean/**

# The whole run tree: 14 GB of production output. This used to live only in
# .git/info/exclude, which is per-clone and never published - so a fresh clone
# elsewhere would have seen runs/ as untracked-but-not-ignored and swept it into
# the next `git add -A`.
runs/

# ------------------------------------------------------- private and copyright
# Supervisor source materials: copyrighted PDFs and an unpublished manuscript.
pshonkin_materials_ishodniki/
# Local notes, drafts and correspondence prepared for the supervisor.
docs/_local/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- session debris
# Reports written by the AI agents that ran the campaign, to hand work between
# sessions. Useful at the time, noise in a published repository.
agent_report*.md
prompt*.txt
pr_body.md
release_commit_manifest.md
# Frozen agent state and verbatim third-party web scrapes.
.codex/
.firecrawl/
# Operator babysitting output: watchdog CSVs, PowerShell transcripts, pagefile
# probes and disk-cleanup manifests. Machine-specific, no scientific content.
diagnostics/
monitor_snapshots/
status_dump_*.txt

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
_docx_build/
*.stackdump
*.tmp
*.temp
*.swp
*.swo
.cache/
.DS_Store

# --------------------------------------------- retired manuscript tooling
# One-shot text patchers from the revision rounds. Every one is a flat list of
# literal replacements whose anchors no longer exist in the sources, so running
# one now does nothing or half-applies. The revision history is in the git log.
docs/paper/revise_*.py
docs/paper/apply_fixes.py
docs/paper/fix_units.py
docs/paper/make_pdf.py
# Superseded reading copies and regenerable packaging. The two current reading
# copies (manuscript_en.pdf, manuscript_ru.pdf) ARE published; the Word and
# Overleaf exports are not - make_docx.py and a zip of the tracked files
# reproduce them in seconds.
docs/paper/main_en_compiled.pdf
docs/paper/main_ru_compiled.pdf
docs/paper/manuscript_en_v2.pdf
docs/paper/manuscript_ru_v2.pdf
docs/paper/manuscript_*_editable.docx
docs/paper/overleaf_*.zip
docs/paper/*.spl

# ------------------------------------------------- correspondence drafts
docs/reports/pshonkin_message_*.md

# ------------------------------- stage F debugging debris (no results in it)
docs/reports/stageF_dual_lane_preflight.*
docs/reports/stageF_gpu_fix_*
docs/reports/stageF_F0_*
docs/reports/*.log
docs/reports/pdf/*.html
docs/reports/pdf/preview_*.png
docs/reports/pdf/stageF_pdf_*

# --------------------------------- third-party archives we do not redistribute
potentials/**/*.tar.gz

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the manuscript
# Published as of the third revision round (4 Sept 2026): sources, figures,
# both reading copies and the drafting apparatus. What stays out is the LaTeX
# build detritus, the spliced intermediates (splice_drafts.py rebuilds
# main_v2.tex / main_ru_v2.tex from main.tex and _drafts/ in one command) and
# the Word/Overleaf exports listed above.
docs/paper/*.aux
docs/paper/*.log
docs/paper/*.out
docs/paper/*.blg
docs/paper/*.toc
docs/paper/main_v2.tex
docs/paper/main_ru_v2.tex
docs/paper/_docx_build/
# Stage B session material that happens to sit in this directory; it has
# nothing to do with the manuscript.
docs/paper/visualization_event_pipeline.md
